  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Sea Rock Light",
    "description": "A striped lighthouse on a rock out in the water, reached only by a footbridge from the shore. Its lantern and windows light up after dark in World View. 35 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — four dark Block 2x2s make a 4x4 rock standing out of the water, two blocks high, with Rocks round it at the waterline and one on the landing by the door.\n2. **Bridge** — from the shore, two Wide Stairs (the upper one on a Brick 1x2, turned 90°) climb to a stone Block 2x2. Two Plate 2x4s, turned 90° (press **R**), cross the water, meeting on a pier of two Round Bricks, with Logs along both sides for handrails. Build the lighthouse with its first step on the shore and the rest out over the water: there is no other way across.\n3. **Tower** — three Block 2x2s stacked white, red, white on the back corner of the rock, so the bridge lands on open stone. The Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; two Small Windows glow with lamplight at night.\n4. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2, a Lantern that lights up after dark, another Round Plate 2x2 and a red Cone Roof.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 4 Block 2x2, 9 Rock\n- Bridge: 2 Wide Stair, 1 Brick 1x2, 1 Block 2x2, 2 Plate 2x4, 2 Round Brick, 4 Log\n- Tower: 3 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 2 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n35 bricks in all.\n",
